Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Jun 17 13:53:12 2025 +0300
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Jun 17 13:53:12 2025 +0300

    Bug 1971694 - Move remaining hardcoded support definitions into annotation files. r=aleca,tobyp


    This is a continuation of the reorganization started in Bug 1970044.
    This patch moves the hardcoded definitions of which Firefox APIs are
    supported by Thunderbird from the webext-compat-data repository [1] into
    annotation files stored in the tree.

    The webext-compat-data repository was helpful to get the work related to
    MDN/BCD, our own WebExtension API linter, and a fully auto-generated
    documentation started, but it will become obsolete. The data generated
    and provided in the webext-schema repository [2] will be our only
    extended source of truth. We still aim to add our Thunderbird related
    compat data to the upstream browser-compat-data (BCD) repository [3],
    which will be sourced from the webext-schemas repository [4] as well.

    ```
         +--------------+        +-----+       +------------------+
         | tree/schemas |        | BCD |       | tree/annotations |
         +--------------+        +-----+       +------------------+
                |                   |                   |
                |                   |                   |
                +----------+        |        +----------+
                           |        |        |
                           v        v        v
                        +-----------------------+
                        |     webext-schemas    |
                        +-----------------------+
                          |      |      |      |
                          |      |      |      |
           +--------------+  +---+      +--+   +-----------+
           |                 |             |               |
           v                 v             v               v
    +-------------+  +---------------+  +-----+  +-------------------+
    | webext-docs |  | webext-linter |  | BCD |  | webext-typescript |
    +-------------+  +---------------+  +-----+  +-------------------+
    ```


    [1]:https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-compat-data/blob/4c6933d3aac0f232ea7bfa5e4e1e748cf6496815/generate_compat_data.js#L74-L99
    [2]:https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-schemas-generator/commit/a17fcabb4e99ac625a38a1b54b429f745969cdb9
    [3]:https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/tree/main/webextensions
    [4]:https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-schemas/tree/beta-mv3

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D253468

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md b/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
index 71c2de7bedc..13eef03b067 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/annotations/README.md
@@ -13,10 +13,19 @@ properties:
 - `hint` - hint string
 - `note` - note string
 - `warning` - warning string
+- `version_added` - a boolean value indicating wether the specified API or property
+is supported by Thunderbird, overriding automatically generated compat data from
+the schema files (schemas read from mail/ default to `true`, schemas read from
+browser/ and toolkit/ default to `false`), can also be an string with a version
+number to override the automatically calculated first supporting version

 Annotation objects may also include `min_manifest_version` and `max_manifest_version`
 properties to specify for which manifest version the annotated information is valid.

+Annotation `note` objects can include a boolean `bcd` property, to indicate that
+the provided annotation should be added to the browser_compat_data [3] repository
+(as `__compat.support.thunderbird.notes`).
+
 The annotation files can also provide `enums` objects with `annotations` arrays
 for the supported enum values.

@@ -28,6 +37,7 @@ or WebExtension linters.

 [1] : https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-schemas-generator
 [2] : https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-schemas
+[3] : https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/tree/main/webextensions

